{
  "title": "iOS CI 'Start server' step passes even when the server never comes up",
  "description": "In .github/workflows/ios.yml the `Start server` step backgrounds ramekin-server and polls /api/test/unauthed-ping for 60s, but the loop just falls through when the server never becomes ready, so the step succeeds. \
The failure then surfaces later as a confusing `Connection refused` in `Seed database`. \
Seen on PR #787 (run 37942965236): on a slow macOS runner (pg_isready took ~55s per poll) the server panicked with `Failed to create database pool: Error(None)` at server/src/db.rs:116, but the step stayed green. \
Fix: exit 1 after the loop if the server never responded (and check the server process is still alive / dump its output), mirroring the mock-openrouter wait step above it. \
Possibly also worth giving the DB pool more connection timeout headroom on CI, or retrying pool creation.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "ci",
    "ios",
  ],
